---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import DraftNotice from '../components/DraftNotice.astro';
import { CONTACT_EMAIL } from '../lib/site';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy"
  description="How the LCR Labs website handles data, and where each application's own privacy behaviour is described."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <header class="head">
        <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
        <h1>Privacy notice</h1>
      </header>

      <div class="prose">
        <DraftNotice
          action="This describes the site as it is currently built and is accurate as far as it goes. It is not a reviewed GDPR/DSGVO privacy policy, and the points below are still open."
        >
          <ul>
            <li>Confirm what GitHub logs as the host, for how long, and on what legal basis</li>
            <li>Confirm the data-processing terms that apply to GitHub Pages</li>
            <li>Add the standard data-subject rights section in German</li>
            <li>Have the finished text reviewed against DSGVO requirements</li>
          </ul>
        </DraftNotice>

        <h2>What this website does</h2>
        <p>
          This site is a set of static pages. It has no accounts, no login, no shop, no
          comment system and no forms. It does not process payments and does not deliver
          software.
        </p>

        <h2>Cookies and tracking</h2>
        <p>
          The site sets no cookies and includes no analytics, advertising or session-replay
          scripts. There is no tracking pixel and no third-party embed.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you use the appearance switch in the header, your choice is stored locally in
          your browser’s local storage under the key <code>lcr-theme</code> and is not
          transmitted by this website.
        </p>

        <h2>Fonts and assets</h2>
        <p>
          All images and styles are served from this site. No web fonts are downloaded — the
          site uses the typefaces already installed on your system — so no font service
          receives your IP address.
        </p>

        <h2>Hosting and server logs</h2>
        <p>
          The site is hosted on GitHub Pages, a service of GitHub, Inc. Its files are served
          from GitHub’s infrastructure, which means GitHub as the host necessarily processes
          the technical data any web server receives when a page is requested — such as your
          IP address, the time of the request, the page requested and your browser’s user
          agent. LCR Labs has no access to raw server logs for this site.
        </p>
        <p>
          What GitHub does with that data is set out in its own <a
            href="https://docs.github.com/en/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-privacy-statement"
            rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub Privacy Statement</a
          >.
        </p>
        <p class="placeholder">
          Retention period, legal basis and the applicable data-processing terms: still to be
          confirmed.
        </p>

        <h2>Outbound links</h2>
        <p>
          Some pages link to services operated by other companies. Following such a link takes
          you to a site under its own privacy policy; nothing about you is passed to it by
          this website beyond what your browser sends on any link.
        </p>

        <h2>Privacy inside the applications</h2>
        <p>
          This notice covers the website only. Each application’s own data handling is
          described on its product page and in the app itself; the shared intent across all
          LCR Labs software is that personal data stays on your Mac.
        </p>

        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>
          For privacy questions, write to <a href={`mailto:${CONTACT_EMAIL}`}>{CONTACT_EMAIL}</a
          >. The responsible party and full contact details are listed in
          the <a href="/imprint/">imprint</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .head {
    margin-bottom: var(--space-10);
  }

  .head h1 {
    margin-top: var(--space-3);
  }

  .placeholder {
    color: var(--text-tertiary);
    font-style: italic;
  }
</style>
